      "message": "I worry about the potential overflow if `offset \u003e table_data.len()`.\n\nI\u0027d write this as (untested):\n```rust\nlet sliced_table_data \u003d font_ref\n    .0\n    .as_ref()\n    .and_then(|f| f.table_data(u32tag_to_tag(tag)))\n    // convert FontData to \u0026[u8]\n    .map(|d| d.as_ref()) \n    .and_then(|bytes| bytes.get(offset..))\n    // this leaves us with any empty slice if any of the above fails,\n    // resulting in copying nothing and returning 0 below\n    .unwrap_or_default(); \nif let Some(sliced_data) \u003d data.get_mut(..sliced_table_data.len()) {\n    sliced_data.copy_from_slice(sliced_table_data);\n    sliced_data.len()\n} else {\n    0\n}\n```\nThis also avoids any potential panics.",
